      <body>
         <entry xml:id="angrotiqah-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אנגרוטיקה</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾngrwṭyqh</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">angroṭiqah</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="pos">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa">אנדרוטיגה</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">ʾndrwṭygh</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic">androṭigah</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="angrotiqah-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>drudgery</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ἀγγερευτικά</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ידיע ליהוי למלכא דיהן קריתא דך תתבנא ושוריא ישתכללון מנדה בלו והלך לא ינתנון מנדה זו מידת הארץ, בלו זו פרוביגרון, והלך 
                     <app>
                        <lem>לאנדרוטיגה</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">לאנגרוטיקה</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1 Ox2">אנגרוטינס</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">לאנגרוטיקא</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">לא יתנון אנגרוטיגה</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V">אנגרוטינה</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">64,10</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 711: 2</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פרוביגרון</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>Be it known now unto the king, that, if this city be builded, and the walls set up again, then will they not pay tribute, impost or toll,(Esr 4,14): “minda” is land tax; “belo” is poll tax; “wa-halakh” means androtiga. (Freedman / Simon II 580)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">bNed 62b</bibl> (<ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">ארנונא</ref>); <bibl type="ancient">bBB 8a</bibl> (<ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">ארנונא</ref>); <bibl type="ancient">EstR petiḥtot 5</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אנגריא</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 111 [34c: 10]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אנגרוטוג</term>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 951 [341d: 3]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">גולגליות</term>), <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 951 [341d: 4]</bibl> (<ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">ארנונא</ref>); <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Esr 1069 [514d: 43]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">גולגלתא</term>) (<ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">ארנונא</ref>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>Suggested already by <bibl type="modern">Dalman 24b</bibl> (<term xml:lang="grc">ἀγγαρευτικά</term>). <bibl type="modern">AC I 138a</bibl>: Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἀγγαρευτής</term>. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 105a</bibl> traces back already to Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἀγγαρεία</term> (cf. <term xml:lang="jpa">אנגריא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾngryʾ</term> in the parallels, and see <bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, DJPA 39b-40a</bibl>, <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 63b</bibl>). <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 63ab</bibl> assumes a composition of <term xml:lang="jpa">אנגריא</term> and <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">אננונא</ref>. See also MY ad loc. The preposition <term xml:lang="jpa">ל</term> is probably a corruption.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Shoval-Dudai</title>
                  <citedRange>39b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
